= Inclusive Hiring Simulation for Policy What-If Analysis
== Abstract
We introduce a simulation microframework for exploring hiring policy effects on utility and inclusion metrics. It provides reproducible scenario analysis and transparent assumptions.

== Method
Agent-based style simulation with configurable screening/interview probabilities by group.

== Experiments
We run a CPU-only benchmark with fixed seed and report accuracy.

== Limitations
Small synthetic/curated data and simplified metrics reduce external validity.

== Ethical Considerations
The tool is intended for decision support; human oversight is required.
